01:03:48,000 --> 01:03:54,000
Us is a 2019 American psychological horror film written and directed by Jordan Peele, and
starring Lupita Nyong'o, Winston Duke, Elisabeth Moss and Tim Heidecker.

12
01:09:36,000 --> 01:09:42,000
The story follows Adelaide Wilson and her family, who are attacked by a
group of menacing doppelgängers, called the "Tethered".

13
01:15:24,000 --> 01:15:30,000
The project was announced in February 2018.

14
01:21:12,000 --> 01:21:18,000
Peele produced the film alongside Jason Blum and Sean McKittrick, having
previously collaborated with them on Get Out and BlacKkKlansman.

15
01:27:00,000 --> 01:27:06,000
Filming took place in California, including Los Angeles,
Pasadena and Santa Cruz, from July to October 2018.

16
01:32:48,000 --> 01:32:54,000
Us premiered at South by Southwest on March 8, 2019, and was theatrically
released in the United States on March 22, by Universal Pictures.

17
01:38:36,000 --> 01:38:42,000
It received widespread critical acclaim, and grossed $256 million against
a budget of $20 million, making it a commercial success.

